+# SWH path, lesson 4 (bottles variant). Design level: build an SWH routine from cards and read the feature report. Built on the SWH guide's worked sequence swh-seq-s5-bottles. Reviewed and published by Steve on 2026-10-08.
+schemaVersion: 1
+id: swh-4-bottles
+path: swh
+track: bottles
+order: 4
+title: "Build it: SWH"
+summary: Build a six-lesson SWH routine for a Year 10 materials unit from activity cards, then read what the guide's look-fors say about it.
+level: design
+version: 1.0.0
+status: published
+lastReviewed: 2026-10-08
+provenance:
+  source: ai-drafted-reviewed
+  authors: [Claude]
+  reviewedBy: [Steve Grant]
+  reviewedOn: 2026-10-08
+context:
+  stages: [stage5]
+  focusAreas: [Materials]
+  disciplines: [chemistry]
+outcomes: [SC5-MAT-01]
+builtOn:
+  sequenceIds: [swh-seq-s5-bottles]
+  lookForIds: [swh-begin-own-question, swh-begin-kept, swh-tests-follows-question, swh-obs-separate, swh-claim-arguable, swh-claim-individual, swh-evidence-justifies, swh-evidence-selected, swh-evidence-anomalies, swh-reading-peers-first, swh-reading-not-answer-key, swh-reading-something-changes, swh-reflect-has-original, swh-reflect-about-thinking]
+  misapplicationIds: [mis-swh-supplied-question, mis-swh-evidence-recopied, mis-swh-answer-key, mis-swh-no-negotiation, mis-swh-lost-beginnings, mis-swh-closed-practical]
+guideSection: checklist
+items:
+  - id: practical
+    type: choice
+    at: beginning-ideas
+    processing: Analysis
+    kind: Choose the practical
+    tests: design
+    title: "Your routine: Year 10, six lessons inside a materials unit. Many students think there's one best material, whatever it's for."
+    q: Which practical gives SWH the most to work with?
+    options:
+      - text: Measuring the density of a steel offcut by displacement
+        fb: One right answer, so claims can't differ and the reading phase has nothing to do. The guide calls this using SWH on a closed practical.
+      - text: Following a printed method to time how fast hot water cools in the steel and glass bottles
+        fb: The method and the comparison are set, so students' own questions have nowhere to go.
+      - text: Four 750 mL bottles (stainless steel, aluminium, glass and a copolyester plastic) and the question of which one the school should choose
+        fb: Yes. Which property matters depends on the purpose, so students' questions and claims can differ, and the reading phase has a real disagreement to work on.
+      - text: Researching bottle materials online and writing a summary
+        fb: There's no practical, so there are no observations of their own to make a claim from.
+    answer: 2
+    refs:
+      misapplicationIds: [mis-swh-closed-practical]
+
+  - id: rubric
+    type: concept
+    at: beginning-ideas
+    processing: Retrieval
+    kind: Before you build
+    title: What the report will look for
+    lead: >-
+      The board checks your plan against the SWH guide's look-fors and misapplications. A card counts only in the
+      phase whose job it does, and some cards look efficient but bring a known problem with them. Leaving out the
+      reading phase, where claims meet other students, is the cut the guide warns about most.
+    rows:
+      - phaseId: beginning-ideas
+        does: Students' own questions, written down and kept.
+        move: "Watch for: a question on the board."
+      - phaseId: tests
+        does: A method that answers their question.
+        move: "Watch for: one method for everyone."
+      - phaseId: observations
+        does: What happened, apart from what it means.
+        move: "Watch for: explaining while recording."
+      - phaseId: claims
+        does: An individual claim someone could disagree with.
+        move: "Watch for: one claim per group."
+      - phaseId: evidence
